{
  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows atropine sulfate injection has been in shortage since 2012-01-01 with multiple manufacturers reporting manufacturing delays and discontinuations",
  "headline_cites": ["D9", "E48", "E43"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage database records the first posting for atropine sulfate injection on 2012-01-01, which is the earliest date its database holds, so the shortage began on or before then.",
      "cites": ["D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira, Inc. (a Pfizer Company) lists manufacturing delay as the reason for its current shortage with next delivery and estimated recovery in December 2026.",
      "cites": ["E48"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Accord Healthcare Inc. reports discontinuation of manufacture for its atropine sulfate injection product.",
      "cites": ["E43"]
    },
    {
      "text": "American Regent, Inc., Amphastar Pharmaceuticals, Inc., Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC, Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc., Medefil, Inc., and Somerset Therapeutics, LLC all show current shortage status on FDA's list.",
      "cites": ["E44", "E45", "E46", "E47", "E49", "E50"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira's plant (FEI 1021343) received OAI classifications in 2010 and 2011, a Warning Letter in 2010-04-12, and its most recent inspection in 2025-02-07 was NAI.",
      "cites": ["E11", "E13", "E15", "E20", "E21"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 1.8 days of 0.1 mg/mL 10 mL syringes on hand while Corvale General has 16.5 days and can spare 10 syringes while maintaining two weeks supply.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The recommended action is to transfer 10 syringes of 0.1 mg/mL 10 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would bring Corvale East to 5 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D10"]
    }
  ]
}
